<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    {% comment %}
      Design tokens, generated from packages/tokens/src/tokens.ts — the same
      source that produces the Tailwind theme for apps/web and apps/mobile.
      Loaded before everything else so merchant settings in 'css-variables'
      and any section styles can override individual values.
    {% endcomment %}
    {{ 'tokens.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

    {% # Inlined CSS Variables %}
    {% render 'css-variables' %}

    {% comment %}
      DM Sans and DM Mono (SHO-110): the same files apps/web serves, synced
      from packages/tokens by `pnpm --filter @formulate/theme build`. Every
      weight loads on demand through @font-face, with font-display: swap.

      The sans weights above the fold are preloaded, so they usually arrive
      before the first paint and the page doesn't jump when they swap in: the
      swap moved the collection page by a CLS of up to 0.08 (budget 0.05),
      depending on how fast the font came. The fallback face's metric
      overrides narrow the jump but can't stop a line rewrapping.

      ⚠️ Preloaded without asset_url's ?v=... query: fonts.css, generated and
      shared with apps/web, asks for each file by a relative URL without one,
      and a preload whose URL doesn't match exactly downloads the font twice.
      DM Mono (prices) isn't preloaded: it's small on the page and the
      preloads already compete with the LCP image.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% # theme-check-disable AssetPreload %}
    {%- assign preloaded_weights = '400,500,600' | split: ',' -%}
    {%- for weight in preloaded_weights -%}
      {%- assign font_file = 'dm-sans-latin-' | append: weight | append: '-normal.woff2' -%}
      <link
        rel="preload"
        href="{{ font_file | asset_url | split: '?' | first }}"
        as="font"
        type="font/woff2"
        crossorigin
      >
    {%- endfor %}
    {% # theme-check-enable AssetPreload %}
    {{ 'fonts.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

    {% # Load and preload the critical CSS %}
    {{ 'critical.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}

    {% # Social, title, etc. %}
    {% render 'meta-tags' %}

    {% # Import map and web components %}
    {% render 'scripts' %}

    {{ content_for_header }}
  </head>

  <body>
    {% comment %}
      First thing on the page, so one Tab reaches it and Enter skips the header
      and its collection links (WCAG 2.4.1, SHO-152). Hidden until focused.
    {% endcomment %}
    <a class="skip-link" href="#MainContent">{{ 'general.skip_to_content' | t }}</a>

    {% sections 'header-group' %}

    {% comment %}
      The page's main landmark, which the theme didn't have. tabindex="-1" so
      the skip link moves focus here, not only the scroll position.
    {% endcomment %}
    <main id="MainContent" tabindex="-1">
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    {% sections 'footer-group' %}

    {% comment %}
      The cart drawer lives in the layout so it is present on every page — a
      shopper can add from a product page and see the drawer without a
      navigation.

      The <dialog> is here rather than inside the section on purpose. Cart
      mutations re-render the section and swap its contents in, and the dialog
      surviving that swap is what preserves its open state, its place in the
      top layer, and any transition mid-flight. Re-rendering the dialog itself
      would close the drawer on every quantity change.
    {% endcomment %}
    <cart-drawer
      data-add-error-label="{{ 'cart.add_error' | t }}"
      data-change-error-label="{{ 'cart.change_error' | t }}"
    >
      <dialog class="cart-drawer" aria-label="{{ 'cart.title' | t }}">
        {% section 'cart-drawer' %}
      </dialog>
    </cart-drawer>
  </body>
</html>
